From cacedca7dadf940071fe8a931026e97704609dcf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 18:52:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] BoardWatch keep: compare the file's schema format
 number too (review of a0f3a0d3cd)

The exact-head review of a0f3a0d3cd (t_ea50320c6a58c33e) approved, with one non-blocking
behaviour point: invariant I5 was still false for one kind of restored image.

Why (the defect):
1. A kept reader answered `v >= 'img-y' ORDER BY v DESC` over a DESC index with no rows,
   where a new connection returns `img-z, img-y`. No error.
2. It walked the index in the wrong direction. A file with schema format number 1 stores a
   DESC index in ascending order; the reader had parsed format 4.
3. The keep let that parse survive: the restored image had the live schema cookie and the
   live `sqlite_schema` rows, which is all the keep compared.
4. The format number is in the database header (bytes 44..47), not in `sqlite_schema`, and
   no statement reports it. The reader's parse holds it all the same.
5. I5 listed what the parse was built from as "cookie and rows". That list was one item short.

Not reachable on today's boards (format 4, no DESC index), but base reopens here and is right.

Fix: `parsed_from(conn, path)` puts the main file's bytes 44..47 in front of `schema_rows`.
Open stores it and the keep compares it. A header that cannot be read is doubt at open and at
the keep: never kept. The bytes come through `sqlite_safe_read.pread_lock_safe`, like the
wal-index baseline, so no descriptor on the board is ever closed.

Cost: one `pread` per open and per keep. A board that has never been checkpointed has no
format number in its main file yet, so its first checkpoint reopens the reader once; after
that it is kept. The live boards all have their header in the main file.

I5 now reads: on keep, the reader drops every unpinned page and its answers, and the file's
schema format number, schema cookie and schema rows must all equal the ones the reader had
at open; otherwise it reopens.

Tests (tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_sync_checkpoint_keep.py, 50 cases, 7 new):
- test_restore_of_another_file_format_under_the_same_schema_reopens: PASSIVE/TRUNCATE x both
  orders. 4 of 4 fail on a0f3a0d3cd's source (the reader is kept) and pass here. Mutant M18.
- test_restored_legacy_format_image_is_read_as_a_fresh_reader_reads_it: the review's case, a
  real format-1 image with a DESC index. Fails under M18 with the wrong rows.
- test_reader_whose_file_header_cannot_be_read_is_not_kept (M19, M20).
- test_board_whose_header_was_only_in_the_wal_reopens_once_then_keeps: the cost above.
- The `board` fixture checkpoints once after its DDL, so its main file has a header, as a
  live board's does. Two existing assertions follow the stored value's new first item.

Proof:
- 21 exact-anchor mutants (M1-M20 and M18b), each killed by its named test.
- Reviewer probe3.py, unchanged, 480 scenarios: 388 SAME, 92 DIFF (was 356 and 124). The 92
  are the same scenarios base 38d25846c0 differs on (the probe's own comparison on corrupt
  images); none is the legacy-format image (was 32).
- Reviewer probe2.py, unchanged: 32 SAME, 0 DIFF. probe3b.py: 48 SAME, 0 DIFF.

Hermes-Card: t_20097f02b6abaa50
